Source: https://github.com/tandryukha/aidemo at b67235a.

What is ported from it here (issue #818, part 1), in Go, in
internal/controlplane/videos/compose: from src/compose.ts, IDLE_CAP_MS, FPS,
MAX_STRETCH, MIN_FACTOR, mergeIdle, sceneAutoIdle, keepIntervals,
offsetInKeeps, the retime, hold and overrun trim of a scene and the remap of
an event through them, extractAndConcat, concatSegments, the "contain" filter
of resizeOutput, overlayPngBatches and the audio of muxAudio (keep.go,
compose.go); from src/ffmpeg.ts, runFfmpeg, probeDurationMs and
probeFreezeSpans (ffmpeg.go); from src/voice.ts, GAP_MS and
assembleNarration (keep.go, compose.go). Each file says what it took, and how
it differs.

Part 2 of issue #818 ports, in Go, from src/captions.ts the cue rules
(DEFAULT_SEG, CONJUNCTIONS, groupWords, splitRun, mergeShort, cueText,
endsClause, endsSentence) into internal/controlplane/videos/captions, and from
src/voice.ts the voice cache (voiceHash and the reuse of a scene's clip) into
internal/controlplane/videos (voice.go).

Issue #908, part 1, takes the "bar" caption style of src/caption-render.ts
(its band color, full width and no rounding) as a preset of
internal/controlplane/videos/captions (presets.go), and its caption flip on a
collision (src/compose.ts) for a tap's ring (styled.go).

Issue #908, part 2, ports, in Go, into internal/controlplane/videos/compose,
from src/frame.ts, frameLayout and the geometry and drawing of
renderFramePng (the device bezel, its border and shadows, the window, the
rounded hole and the camera cut-outs), with the frame defaults of
src/types.ts (frame.go, plate.go); and from src/compose.ts the frame pass
that pads the picture and overlays the frame's PNG (compose.go). The goldens'
script, compose/testdata/frames/render.mjs, uses renderFramePng's HTML.
